# 2. Scope

## Scope Statement

This document defines the governance framework for all System Objectives developed within the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA).

Its scope covers the complete management lifecycle of System Objectives, from their creation through approval, maintenance, traceability, version control, and retirement.

---

## In Scope

This document governs:

- The classification of System Objectives.
- Objective identification and naming conventions.
- Objective lifecycle management.
- Objective ownership and responsibilities.
- Objective relationships and hierarchy.
- Objective traceability.
- Objective change management.
- Objective approval and review processes.
- Objective version control.
- Objective retirement and archival.
- Compliance requirements for all objective documentation.

---

## Out of Scope

This document does not govern:

- Project governance.
- The System Objective Specification (SOS).
- The technical content of individual objectives.
- System requirements.
- System architecture.
- Detailed engineering design.
- Verification procedures.
- Validation procedures.
- Project management processes.

These subjects are governed by their respective engineering documents.

---

## Scope Boundary

This document governs **how System Objectives are managed**, not **what the objectives are**.

The definition of objectives remains the responsibility of the objective category documents, while the governance of those objectives remains the responsibility of this document.

---

## Relationship to Parent and Child Documents

This document operates under the authority of the System Objective Specification (SOS) and provides governance to all objective category documents within the `objectives/` subdomain.

It serves as the management layer between the governing specification (SOS) and the detailed objective definitions.
